	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Translator

en &lt;text&gt;: translate detected input to en-US and show result in Alfred.
zh &lt;text&gt;: translate detected input to zh-TW and show result in Alfred.
// add or delete whatever language keyword you want

Result rows show the Shortcut output directly.
Press Return on the result row to copy.

Shortcut mode uses Input File by default and matches Shortcuts that read Shortcut Input.
DeepL and OpenAI remain optional providers. Only Shortcut provider supports custom language.

Shortcut structure:

1. Shortcut Input: Files, Clipboard, Text
2. Make Rich text from Markdown: {Shortcut Input}
3. Text: {Rich text from Markdown}
4. Translate {Text} from {Detected Language} to {Chinese (Mandarin - Taiwan)} // or other language you want
5. Text: {Translated Text}
6. Stop and Output {Text}

Tip: Execute `shortcuts list` to make sure the names of your shortcuts.</string>
